# Multi-day festival When

Short multi-day festivals (not long seasonal farms) use `scheduleKind: 'multi-day'` with `openingDate` + `closingDate`.

## Event page WHEN

**When the next day is today or tomorrow**

```
Tomorrow, September 5
8:00 AM–5:00 PM
During Labor Day weekend · Sep 5–7
```

(`scheduleWindowLabel` + range on the third line when set.)

**When the span is further out**

```
Sep 19–20
Sat–Sun · 11:00 AM–5:00 PM
```

(No third line unless `scheduleWindowLabel` is set.)

## Browse card

Status + hours only (same spirit as seasonal-run): relative day or span as primary, hours as secondary. Omit the “During …” window line on cards.

## Fields

| Field | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `openingDate` / `closingDate` | Inclusive festival dates |
| `recurringDaysLabel` | e.g. `Sat–Sun` when helpful; omit or Daily when every day in a short window |
| `scheduleWindowLabel` | e.g. `During Labor Day weekend` → third WHEN line with the date range |

## Tips

Do not restate the weekend dates/hours in Good to know — see `tips-no-when-duplication.mdc`.

